{"additions":403,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPart of #148, closes #149.\n\n- `fetch_board` now also fetches the project's **saved views** (`ProjectV2.views` via `gh api graphql` — the `gh project` CLI does not expose them): name, layout (`TABLE` / `BOARD` / `ROADMAP`), filter expression, `groupByFields` / `verticalGroupByFields` / `sortByFields` and the visible fields, resolved by field name. User and organization projects both work (root chosen from the linked project's `resourcePath`, with a try-both fallback).\n- Views live on `Board` (`#[serde(default)]`, so old `board-<n>.json` caches still load) and share the board's disk cache and staleness handling. A views fetch failure is non-fatal — the board still loads and the page keeps today's fixed `Status` kanban.\n- **`v` / `V`** on the board cycle the saved views; the header shows `Board: <project> · <view> [layout] (i/n)`. A refresh of the same project keeps the shown view; switching projects starts on their first view. With no views, `v` explains instead.\n- Rendering each layout the way the view defines it is the follow-up work (#150 Table, #151 Board, #152 Roadmap, #153 filter).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Verified live against the demo project (header shows `· View 1 [table]` in the re-recorded GIF).\n- Adding Board / Roadmap views to the demo project via `createProjectV2View` was blocked by the local permission gate — to demo multi-view cycling in #150+, the views need to be added from the web UI (or the mutation approved).\n\n## Tests\n\n`ViewLayout` parsing, old-cache compatibility + serde round-trip, and `v` / `V` cycling (no views → message, wrap-around, view kept across same-project refresh, reset on project switch). 357 tests green, clippy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":14,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-03T09:30:04Z","deletions":9,"headRefName":"feat/projects-views","labels":[],"number":159,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABL_9nsw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe docs contain incorrect issue links and the GraphQL query imposes low hard limits that can silently truncate saved views/metadata.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds support for fetching GitHub Projects (v2) **saved views** via GraphQL and introduces keybindings to cycle through them on the Projects board, with header/UI updates and accompanying documentation updates. This extends the Projects page toward reproducing GitHub’s Table/Board/Roadmap view definitions while remaining read-only and maintaining existing cache behavior.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Fetch `ProjectV2.views` (name/number/layout/filter/grouping/sorting/visible fields) alongside board fields/items and store them in the existing board cache format.\n- Add `v` / `V` bindings to cycle saved views and show the current view name/layout in the Projects header.\n- Update user docs/config reference and re-record the Projects demo GIF.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Passes owner kind through to board fetch so view GraphQL can query user vs org projects correctly. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Adds view cycling actions/state (`view_idx`), header label helpers, and tests for cycling behavior. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Introduces saved view data types (`ProjectView`, `ViewLayout`, `ViewSort`) and persists them on `Board` with backward-compatible deserialization. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/disk_cache.rs | Updates board cache round-trip test to include the new `views` field. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/client.rs | Fetches saved views via `gh api graphql` and merges them into `fetch_board`. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Renders the current saved view name/layout (and position) in the Projects header. |\r\n| README.md | Documents `v` / `V` keybindings for Projects. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README keybinding documentation update for `v` / `V`. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Adds “Saved views” section and keybinding entry. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-reference.md | Adds `NextView` / `PrevView` actions to Projects config reference. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese “Saved views” guide section and keybinding entry. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md | Japanese Projects config reference update for view cycling actions. |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Updates recorded demo asset to reflect the new header/UI. |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds default bindings for `v` / `V` on the Projects board pane. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 14/14 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-03T09:34:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"68bcffeaa19465a2e4325040b64ff13f1429989e"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMAApYw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"84d6db56ae0ca746ea6c56925da7aa4310cbb3c8"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMAAq9A","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"84d6db56ae0ca746ea6c56925da7aa4310cbb3c8"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMAAsbQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"84d6db56ae0ca746ea6c56925da7aa4310cbb3c8"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMADewQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere are documented, user-visible issues (broken Markdown code spans) and a confirmed correctness risk from identifying projects/boards only by `number`, which can mis-fetch/mis-cache when user/org projects share the same number.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/projects/panes/board.rs:231**\n* `set_board` decides whether this is “the same project” by comparing only `board.number`. Since project numbers are not globally unique across user/org owners, switching between two projects with the same number would incorrectly preserve `view_idx` instead of resetting to the first view.\n**src/projects/state.rs:274**\n* `spawn_board` looks up the project owner by matching only `p.number == number`. ProjectV2 numbers are per-owner (user/org), so if two linked projects share a number this can pick the wrong owner and fetch/cache the wrong board/views.\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 14/14 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-03T09:42:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"84d6db56ae0ca746ea6c56925da7aa4310cbb3c8"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T10:57:33Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33747079960/job/100621964061","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-03T10:57:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T09:40:14Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33739980429/job/100599372405","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:44Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T09:39:36Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33739980510/job/100599372449","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T09:39:48Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33739980429/job/100599372276","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:45Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T09:40:52Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33739980429/job/100599372019","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T09:40:53Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33739980429/job/100600021450","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-09-03T09:40:53Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T10:57:33Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33747079960/job/100621954910","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-09-03T10:57:41Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T09:39:55Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33739980510/job/100599372257","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T09:40:07Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33739980510/job/100599372575","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-03T09:38:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-03T10:57:33Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33747079960/job/100621919420","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-09-03T10:57:33Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Projects: fetch saved views and switch between them (v / V)"}
